 subject="comment 2"
 date="2026-03-24T11:55:06Z"
 content="""
I've since tested, and this does indeed work to suppress the messages about missing files during DNF transactions, in place of the code quoted above (from lines 41-44 of `/etc/etckeeper/post-install/50vcs-commit`):

```bash
        if [ \"$LOWLEVEL_PACKAGE_MANAGER\" = rpm ]; then
                # messages about missing files are sent to stderr
                get_changes | sed 's/^/\/etc\//;s/\s*$//' | xargs -d '\n' rpm 2>/dev/null --qf '%{NAME}\n' -qf
        fi
```

"""]]
